es agreement, so use **have to restore**."}}},{"id":"db08e216-3020-5497-ae27-cbcc82b609c0","topicSlug":"modal-obligation","level":"B1","prompt":"The rule forbids the task. “You ____ measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"do not have to"},{"id":"B","text":"may"},{"id":"C","text":"should"},{"id":"D","text":"must not"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Decide whether the instruction means **forbidden** or merely **not required**.","explanation":"**Must not** means the action is forbidden, matching the explicit rule.","keywords":["prohibition"],"skill":"prohibition","contextKey":"modal-obligation-3","fingerprint":"ac1a25e556ad993fcf839f663d0bbae04a8c09034fd641603a2760d8da96fa1d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-obligation"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Decide whether the instruction means **forbidden** or merely **not required**.","**Must not** means the action is forbidden, matching the explicit rule.","Choose **must not**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This means the task is optional, not forbidden.","B":"May would give permission or possibility.","C":"Should recommends the task, opposite to the prohibition.","D":"**Must not** means the action is forbidden, matching the explicit rule."}}},{"id":"17de2b14-ffb6-5f0c-a9a8-dac2ea598e45","topicSlug":"modal-obligation","level":"B1","prompt":"The task is optional and allowed. “You ____ measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"must not"},{"id":"B","text":"must"},{"id":"C","text":"have to"},{"id":"D","text":"do not have to"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Optional means **no obligation**, not prohibition.","explanation":"**Do not have to** means there is no obligation; the task remains allowed.","keywords":["no-obligation"],"skill":"no-obligation","contextKey":"modal-obligation-3","fingerprint":"b5b3efa